{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REGRESSION-SAFETY CHECK for the EARLY LAND (required by the skill's early-land exception; recorded BEFORE submitting).\n\nCONDITION 1 — every change green on every gate. VERIFIED just now via the Gerrit REST API, all four:\n  1010 (J2)  LLM-Review +1  Verified +1  submittable=True\n  1011 (J4)  LLM-Review +1  Verified +1  submittable=True\n  1013 (J3)  LLM-Review +1  Verified +1  submittable=True\n  1015 (J5)  LLM-Review +1  Verified +1  submittable=True\n0 unresolved comments on each. Each earned Verified independently across the 4-entry CI matrix (ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 + macos py3.13).\n\nCONDITION 2 — will not cause regression. Reasoned, and tested against the ACTUAL merge result rather than an approximation:\n * main has NOT moved since I branched: origin/main is still 7fc96b277 (J1), my HEAD adds exactly 4 commits, and main holds 0 commits I lack. So my worktree IS the merge result — no rebase, no divergence. The full suite I ran (7595 passed / 29 skipped / 0 failed, 27m48s) executed against precisely the tree that will land. That is the strongest form this check can take.\n * BLAST RADIUS, per change:\n   - J2 is a relocation. Behavior-preserving except ONE declared change, and J1's held-out characterization oracle passes with its assertions UNMODIFIED across it. The declared change (deleted -> 'Done') is send-side and in-memory, never writes the local store, and REPLACES an invalid transition name ('Deleted') that is not a state in the live workflow — so the prior behavior never successfully transitioned anything. Strictly a fix.\n   - J4 adds a module and makes Cloud delegate to it. The state machine is asserted EQUAL TO THE LIVE BACKEND across all 7 documented states, both sides evaluated at runtime, so drift is impossible without failing.\n   - J3 adds codec modules. Cloud's two distinct rich-text paths (sanitizer = fit only; send path = fit then normalize) are preserved and mutation-proven; collapsing them fails a held-out test.\n   - J5 is PURELY ADDITIVE and touches no src/ at all: a new test-only directory the default suite excludes by construction (verified: collect-only yields 0), a new CI job, a Makefile target, and a single --ignore flag narrowing one weekly job to exclude only the new directory.\n * NO store, schema, migration, or persisted-data change anywhere in the four. Nothing requires a data migration to revert.\n * REVERSIBILITY: each change is a single commit revertable with git revert; the only behavioral one (J2's deleted key) restores cleanly with no cleanup pass.\n\nWHY EARLY AT ALL: J5's acceptance evidence requires dispatching the new external-integration job, which cannot run until the job EXISTS ON main (workflow_dispatch only, and GitHub is a read-only mirror so no side branch is possible). Landing is therefore a precondition of verification, not a shortcut around it. J5 stays OPEN until the dispatched run actually passes.\n\nCHECK CLEARED. Submitting 1015, which submits its ancestors 1013, 1011, 1010 in order."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785377386170494001,"uuid":"09a57515-0225-4474-a345-58781d035463"}